> f(x,y) = (2*x^2+3*x*y+y^2)/(x^2+y^2)
> limit f(x,0) x->inf
limit of 2x^2/x^2 as x -> inf:
  leading terms: 2*x^2 / (1*x^2)
  = 2
  numeric (x = 10*2^k, k = 0..21): 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2
    extrapolated (Richardson): 2 (estimated error 0): agrees
> limit f(x,x) x->inf
limit of (2x^2 + 3x*x + x^2)/(x^2 + x^2) as x -> inf:
  leading terms: 6*x^2 / (2*x^2)
  = 3
  numeric (x = 10*2^k, k = 0..21): 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3
    extrapolated (Richardson): 3 (estimated error 0): agrees
> limit f(x,2*x) x->inf
limit of (2x^2 + 3x*2x + (2x)^2)/(x^2 + (2x)^2) as x -> inf:
  leading terms: 12*x^2 / (5*x^2)
  = 12/5
  numeric (x = 10*2^k, k = 0..21): 2.4, 2.4, 2.4, 2.4, 2.4, 2.4
    extrapolated (Richardson): 2.4 (estimated error 0): agrees
> limit f(x,-x) x->inf
limit of (2x^2 - 3x*x + (-x)^2)/(x^2 + (-x)^2) as x -> inf:
  = 0
  numeric (x = 10*2^k, k = 0..21): 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0
    extrapolated (Richardson): 0 (estimated error 0): agrees
> g(x,y) = (x^3+y^3)/(x^2+y^2)
> limit g(x,x) x->inf
limit of (x^3 + x^3)/(x^2 + x^2) as x -> inf:
  leading terms: 2*x^3 / (2*x^2)
  = inf
  numeric (x = 10*2^k, k = 0..21): 10, 160, 2560, 40960, 655360, 20971520
    the values grow without bound (+): agrees
